    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Regular simple future",
     "texto": [
      "**-ei, -ás, -á, -emos, -ão**: **falar** → **falarei** (I will speak), **comer** → **comerei** (I will eat), **partir** → **partirei** (I will leave).",
      "The same as in Spanish, but the endings are written attached."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Ir + infinitive or simple future",
     "texto": [
      "In everyday conversation **vou falar** (I'm going to speak) is very common. The simple future appears more in careful texts and also serves for predictions and announcements: **Amanhã falarei com a diretora** (tomorrow I will speak with the director)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
